q. toolchain: exit 0 | cannot find "v" in PATH -> accepted; invalid toolchain "v" in <file> | invalid GOTOOLCHAIN "v" -> rejected; else unknown. go: exit 0 | TooNew echoing v -> accepted/too-new; invalid go version 'v': | the fixed missing-go-root-module abort -> rejected; else unknown.\n\nAlso closed the go-directive classifier, beyond the directive: its fall-through named rejection, which launders an unrelated failure just as effectively for any value the isolated measurement already rejects, where the two would again agree for the wrong reason. Requiring the echoed name is load-bearing beyond tidiness: Select renders two further invalid GOTOOLCHAIN %q messages that quote the ENVIRONMENT value (local+path), never the go.mod name; those now fall to unknown, correctly.\n\nNew expected-red control -red unrelated-command-failure restores the retired `go build ./...` form, so the injected unrelated failure is one upstream really produces for two shape-valid isolated-representable names, not a fabricated error string. Controls are now four.\n\nDocs: reference 4.2.1.2 corroborating bullet split into five with the closure and narrowest-command requirements and both recognised sets; run record gains the fourth carrying measurement; control table 3 -> 4; section 8 gains 127c (classifier is closed) and moves controls to 127d. Decision 0007 section 4 gains the closure requirement with the measured evidence; two new rejected alternatives (fall-through to a verdict, rejected in BOTH directions; keeping go build and widening the recognised set); TASK-260728-2jaw7h obligation now four controls plus closed classifier plus narrowest-command rule; reserved rust/swift/kotlin/jdk each owe their own closed set, since cargo, swift build and Gradle all run substantial work after their version check. CHANGELOG one bullet extended.\n\nGates, standalone, real exit codes: validate 0 (42 schemas / 422 vector files), unittest 0 (29), go test 0, go vet 0, gofmt 0 no output, git diff --check 0 n